build: link xdg-user-dirs-update with libiconv where iconv is not in libc

xdg-user-dirs-update converts directory names from UTF-8 to the
filename_encoding of user-dirs.conf with iconv_open()/iconv(). The meson
build links only libintl: on QNX iconv is not part of libc but a library of
its own (libiconv, whose <iconv.h> renames the functions to libiconv_open,
libiconv), and the link fails with undefined references. Ask meson for its
"iconv" dependency, which is empty where libc has the functions and
-liconv where it does not.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
   libintl_dep = cc.find_library('intl', required: true)
 endif
 
+# iconv: in libc on glibc/musl, a library of its own (libiconv) elsewhere
+iconv_dep = dependency('iconv', required: false)
+if not iconv_dep.found()
+  iconv_dep = declare_dependency()
+endif
+
 systemd_dep = dependency('systemd', required: false)
 
 #
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 xdg_user_dirs_update = executable('xdg-user-dirs-update',
   'xdg-user-dirs-update.c',
   include_directories: config_inc,
-  dependencies: [libintl_dep],
+  dependencies: [libintl_dep, iconv_dep],
   install: true
 )
 
